3. Ontology and evidence status

The two-axis classification is retained. A variable is placed on the physical axis (\mathcal{E} environment, \mathcal{P} production, \mathcal{S} storage, \mathcal{D} decision) and on the epistemic axis (E1 observed, E2 inferred, E3 simulated). Two clarifications are added.

First, V_{\mathrm{op}}(s) from E-0789 is E1 as a bus voltage and E2 as a power-producing capability, because a bus voltage is not a maximum-power-point voltage. Every table reporting power must carry this distinction.

Second, \tau(s) is E3 in this study. No independent high-cadence optical-depth retrieval is assumed to be co-archived with the array currents. Approach P is therefore confined to scenario generation and to the transfer test of §8, never to empirical validation.

