7.4 Temporal validity

Policies are \mathcal{F}_s-measurable. Splitting is by episode, not by sol: each dust event, together with a declared pre- and post-window, is assigned wholly to one fold. In particular, the 2018 global event is assigned wholly to a held-out fold. Global events are autocorrelated over tens of sols; sol-level splitting leaks. Bootstrap resampling is by episode, not by sol, so that dependence within an event is preserved. Any violation invalidates the affected result.

