9. Refutation protocol

Thresholds denoted \square are instantiated and timestamped in a pre-registration record after the audit of §10 and before any evaluation.

Test Refutation condition Consequence
K1 — Antecedence A published method covers the same functional chain with comparable results Originality claim withdrawn
K2 — Forecast Brier skill against persistence <\delta_{\mathrm{B}} on held-out episodes H1a rejected
K3 — Calibration \mathrm{Rel}^{\mathrm{CORP}}>\varepsilon or systematic underestimation of deficit probability Model inadmissible as a safety estimator
K4 — Decision Critical deficit higher than reference at matched sacrifice H2 rejected
K5 — Transfer Opportunity-equivalent forcing does not reproduce the published collapse Tail declared not reproducible; validity domain restricted
K6 — Data Essential variables not reconstructable without arbitrary assumptions; or E-0789 co-observed subset too small or too biased Limit analysis published, not a controller
K7 — Monotonicity Reliability non-monotone in severity or missingness H3 rejected; failure structure reported
K8 — Tail safety \Delta_{\mathrm{tail}}^{\mathrm{CORP}}>\varepsilon_{\mathrm{tail}} with episode-bootstrap lower bound above \varepsilon_{\mathrm{tail}} Model declared unsafe for operational reserve estimation in dust-storm conditions, irrespective of bulk calibration
K9 — Thermal fragility Conclusion reverses sign across the declared \kappa_{T} band Result reported as fragile; no operational recommendation
K10 — Confound Conclusion reverses sign when the deposition model is set to \hat D\equiv 1 Result reported as confounded by array deposition; no dust-predictability claim
