10. Data manifest and work order

10.1 Manifest specification

The audit produces a per-sol table with at least the following columns:

\texttt{sol},\ \texttt{K}_s,\ \rho_{\mathrm{noon}},\ \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}},\ \texttt{E0771\_avail},\ \texttt{E0791\_avail},\ \texttt{E0789\_avail},\ \texttt{E0789\_cadence},\ V_{\mathrm{op}},\ \sigma_{V},\ \hat D,\ \lambda,\ \texttt{episode\_id},\ \texttt{bundle\_url}.

The manifest covers sols 0–200 and the 2022 storm episodes, because the 2022 window is the only period in which the reference policy can be retrodicted against an observed operational trigger.

10.2 Work order

1. Freeze the definitions of §4–§5: geometry normalisation, noon window, deposition model, thermal band, failure events, measurability.
2. Audit the InSight engineering archive at file level. Verify, by direct inspection of the ancillary files, whether E-0789 is co-sampled with E-0771/E-0791 or archived at housekeeping cadence. Do not assume; the manifest column must be filled from the files.
3. Characterise the co-observed subset and report the selection effect on the \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}} distribution.
4. Fix the deposition band \lambda\in[0.05,2]\,\%/\mathrm{sol} with InSight-specific central alternatives, and pre-register the confound test K10.
5. Build the first-order simulator with the thermal band of §5.2, the environment-coupled critical load of §5.3, and the intra-sol resolution required for \mathcal{D}^{E}.
6. Run the transfer test of §8 before any decision comparison; a failure there invalidates the tail and restricts the claim.
7. Run the three-stage oracle gate of §6.4; report \Delta_{\mathrm{oracle}} and the conditional VoI before touching H2.
8. Compare policies on paired environmental realisations, with the robustness clause H2-R.
9. Execute K8, K9, K10, K11 and report each as passed, failed, or inconclusive.
10. Freeze the claim only after a novelty audit against the array-current analyses, the MER opacity retrievals, the probabilistic dust-forecast literature, and the integrated task-planning literature.

