Appendix D — Non-mixing and circularity

D.1 Invariance of approach O under non-multiplication

Proposition D.1. Let \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}} be defined from measured currents i_j that already contain the true atmospheric and deposition attenuation. Then the choice

P_{\mathrm{pv}}^{\mathrm{(O)}}(s)=\alpha\,\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}(s)\,V_{\mathrm{op}}(s)

is the unique choice consistent with the definition of \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}, up to a calibrated \alpha. Applying an additional dust factor \mathrm{DF}(s) produces

P'^{\mathrm{(O)}}(s)=\alpha\,\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}(s)\,V_{\mathrm{op}}(s)\,\mathrm{DF}(s),

and \mathbb{E}[P'^{\mathrm{(O)}}]=\mathbb{E}[P^{\mathrm{(O)}}]\,\mathbb{E}[\mathrm{DF}]\neq\mathbb{E}[P^{\mathrm{(O)}}] whenever \mathbb{E}[\mathrm{DF}]\neq 1.

Proof. Write \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}=cGTD\varepsilon. Then P^{\mathrm{(O)}}=\alpha cGTD\varepsilon V_{\mathrm{op}} is the physically correct power (up to calibration). Multiplying by \mathrm{DF} yields P'^{\mathrm{(O)}}=P^{\mathrm{(O)}}\cdot\mathrm{DF}, which is not equal in expectation to P^{\mathrm{(O)}} unless \mathbb{E}[\mathrm{DF}]=1. Since \mathrm{DF}\in(0,1] and \mathrm{DF}<1 when attenuation is non-zero, the double counting is strict. \square

D.2 Circularity check

Proposition D.2. Suppose the physical model P uses a \tau-retrieval \hat\tau obtained from the same currents that define \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}. Then P is circular for empirical evaluation: the model becomes a tautology P^{\mathrm{(P)}}=f(\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}), and any agreement between P and observation is definitional rather than empirical.

Proof. Let \hat\tau=g(i_1,i_2) be the retrieval, and \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}=h(i_1,i_2) the proxy. If both g and h are invertible (or monotone), then \hat\tau=g\circ h^{-1}(\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}), so P^{\mathrm{(P)}}=\eta A F_0 G\exp(-g(h^{-1}(\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}))/\mu)\mathrm{DF}, which is a deterministic function of \varphi_{\mathrm{noon}}. Agreement with observation follows identically. \square

Implementation. The correlation test r(\varphi_{\mathrm{noon}},\hat\tau) on the sols where P is proposed; a value |r|>\varepsilon_r (with \varepsilon_r pre-declared) triggers the circularity rejection, and P is confined to the simulator.

