Appendix H — Transfer test

H.1 Diffuse-dominance lower bound

Proposition H.1. Let P_{\mathrm{true}}=P_{\mathrm{direct}}+P_{\mathrm{diffuse}}, with P_{\mathrm{direct}}=\eta A F_0 G\exp(-\tau/\mu) and P_{\mathrm{diffuse}}>0. Let P_{\mathrm{sim}}=P_{\mathrm{direct}}. Then P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\tau)\le P_{\mathrm{true}}(\tau) for all \tau, with strict inequality whenever P_{\mathrm{diffuse}}>0. Consequently, the simulated collapse ratio satisfies

\frac{P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\tau_{\mathrm{post}})}{P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\tau_{\mathrm{pre}})}\;\le\;\frac{P_{\mathrm{true}}(\tau_{\mathrm{post}})}{P_{\mathrm{true}}(\tau_{\mathrm{pre}})}

whenever P_{\mathrm{diffuse}} increases faster in \tau than P_{\mathrm{direct}} decreases.

Proof. The pointwise inequality is immediate. For the ratio, note that P_{\mathrm{true}}=P_{\mathrm{direct}}(1+\rho(\tau)) with \rho=P_{\mathrm{diffuse}}/P_{\mathrm{direct}} increasing in \tau. Then P_{\mathrm{true}}(\tau_{\mathrm{post}})/P_{\mathrm{true}}(\tau_{\mathrm{pre}})=P_{\mathrm{direct}}(\tau_{\mathrm{post}})/P_{\mathrm{direct}}(\tau_{\mathrm{pre}})\cdot(1+\rho(\tau_{\mathrm{post}}))/(1+\rho(\tau_{\mathrm{pre}})), and the second factor exceeds one, so the true ratio exceeds the simulated ratio. \square

H.2 Transfer test as falsification

Corollary H.2.1. If the published collapse ratio is R_{\mathrm{pub}} and the simulator produces R_{\mathrm{sim}}, then:

(i) If R_{\mathrm{sim}}>R_{\mathrm{pub}}(1+\delta_R) for a pre-declared tolerance \delta_R, the simulator overestimates post-collapse production and its tail physics is inadmissible.

(ii) If R_{\mathrm{sim}}<R_{\mathrm{pub}}(1-\delta_R), the simulator underestimates post-collapse production, consistent with the diffuse-light omission, and the tail is declared not reproducible on the strength of the current physics.

(iii) Otherwise the transfer test passes and the tail claim is admitted, conditionally on the declared tolerance and the declared forcing.

Proof. Direct from H.1 and the definition of the tolerance. \square

