J.2 Detrending pipeline (pseudocode)

```
Inputs: i1(s,k), i2(s,k), mu(s,k), m(s,k)
1. For each sol s: k_noon(s) = argmax_{k: m=1} mu(s,k)
   with the noon-window constraint |ell - ell_noon| <= Delta_ell.
2. phi_noon(s) = 0.5 * sum_j i_j(s,k_noon(s)) / i_j^ref  if m(s,k_noon)=1 else NaN.
3. G(s) = (R_bar / R(s))^2.
4. Fit (c, lambda, J) on the training episode set by minimising
   sum_s (log phi_noon(s) - log c - log G(s) - log D_hat(s;lambda,J))^2
   subject to D_hat monotone and J >= 0 on declared cleaning sols.
5. r(s) = log phi_noon(s) - log G(s) - log D_hat(s).
6. Report r(s) under (lambda_0, J_hat) and under D_hat ≡ 1.
7. Flag confound (K10) if the sign of any downstream conclusion reverses.
```

J.3 Oracle-gated VoI (pseudocode)

```
Stage 1 (oracle):
  Compute C(pi_ref) and C(pi_oracle) on paired environmental realisations.
  Delta_oracle = C(pi_ref) - C(pi_oracle).
  If Delta_oracle <= Delta_min: declare forecast-irrelevant; stop.

Stage 2 (conditional VoI):
  For each s, evaluate u_ref(s), u_DP(s), set A(s) = 1{u_ref != u_DP}.
  VoI = E[C | pi_ref, A=1] - E[C | pi_DP, A=1].
  If VoI <= 0: report structural irrelevance on the disagreement set; stop.

Stage 3 (decision comparison):
  Compare C(pi_DP) vs C(pi_ref) on paired environmental realisations.
  Report H2 pass/fail and H2-R (95th-percentile deficit).
```

J.4 Transfer test (pseudocode)

```
Inputs: Opportunity 2018 forcing tau*(t), published power series (P0, PT, T).
1. Run simulator on tau*(t) with declared initial state E_0, P_crit, P_non.
2. Compute R_sim = P_sim(T) / P_sim(0).
3. Compute R_pub = PT / P0.
4. If R_sim > R_pub * (1 + delta_R): reject simulator tail (overestimate).
5. If R_sim < R_pub * (1 - delta_R): reject simulator tail (underestimate).
6. Else: transfer test passes; tail claim admitted, conditional on declared tolerance.
```

